  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Electronic configuration of divalent metal ion having atomic number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn></math> is</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/bdbb56db-49f7-4af7-9601-387b41f43d96-image.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 52px;\" /></p><p>Total number of unpaired electrons<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi></math> (Magnetic moment) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></msqrt><mi>BM</mi></math></p><p>where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo></math> number of unpaired <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>35</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>92</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p>",
